  "title": "CHAPTER 1: HISTORY OF MAHARASHTRA",
  "order": 1,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "t8gojp3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1.1 Ancient History of Maharashtra"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Ancient Maharashtra was ruled by key dynasties including the Satavahana Dynasty and Yadava Dynasty (850 CE – 1317 CE).",
        "The Bahmani Sultanate (1347–1527 CE) was a major medieval power in the region.",
        "Chhatrapati Shivaji Maharaj established the Maratha Empire and introduced the Ashtapradhan (Council of Eight Ministers).",
        "Maharashtra played a pivotal role in the Indian Freedom Movement, marked by the Anglo-Maratha Wars and prominent Social Reform Movements."
      ],
      "id": "60ll89z"
    },
